  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "review-e93de9787959-1-review-1",
      "kind": "blocking",
      "status": "resolved",
      "acceptance_id": "DAL-S5-A1",
      "source": "review",
      "review_round": 1,
      "summary": "The agreed seam (both Hosts, counting gate stub) is replaced by a direct call to the host-neutral relayLaneDecision. Nothing tests the Claude ClaudeRuntime.authorize relay, the Pi relayPiLaneDecision relay, the 'exactly one native gate' count, the lane_decision_required report field, the end-to-end breaking-revision rebind, or the Initiative-child refusal.",
      "anchor": "sha256:6367bc46eb97957071bba1d20ff4708d97d4ca1ec53688cf78f3f32377b922ff",
      "evidence": {
        "trigger": "tests/single-task-lane-decision.test.ts imports only relayLaneDecision, laneDecisionFacts, rebindSingleTaskIdentity and startBatch. Its relay input uses a hand-written apply() closure, so the gate is never a Host gate and no counting stub is used. There is no ClaudeRuntime or Pi tool case. startBatch is never driven to a lane_decision_required report. approve_breaking_intent_revision is never relayed, because rebindSingleTaskIdentity is called directly. No test relays against an Initiative batch child through a Host entry (the only negative is a repo with no batch at all). The Host wiring at kernel_ports.ts (authorize, with applied: state !== 'replan_selected') and imm-canary-work.ts (relayPiLaneDecision, with applied: state === 'applied' and a Lane-rooted ctx) can therefore regress with no failing test. Observable wrong result: a Host that opens zero or two gates, applies in the Parent checkout instead of the Lane root, or omits lane_decision_required still passes the suite.",
        "caller_chain": [
          "tests/single-task-lane-decision.test.ts",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/claude/kernel_ports.ts#ClaudeRuntime.authorize",
          "plugins/immune-brain/.pi-extension/imm-canary-work.ts#relayPiLaneDecision",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/lane_decision.ts#relayLaneDecision",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/batch_runner.ts#superviseSingle"
        ],
        "violated": {
          "kind": "acceptance",
          "ref": "DAL-S5-A1"
        }
      },
      "counterevidence": null
    },
    {
      "id": "review-e93de9787959-2-review-2",
      "kind": "blocking",
      "status": "resolved",
      "acceptance_id": "DAL-S5-A2",
      "source": "review",
      "review_round": 1,
      "summary": "A2's cancelled-stop-gate case and the Host-level stop relay are not tested. The stop test supplies a default apply that always reports applied and never exercises a native stop gate.",
      "anchor": "sha256:4171629972c056a7dc0b1dbe19b246075b83bb32f867eb0d2a5ede779219aede",
      "evidence": {
        "trigger": "In the 'stops the live generation after a relayed Kernel stop' test, apply is the default stub (applied.value = true, returns {state:'applied'}). No test relays operation 'stop' with a cancelled or failed gate and asserts the Lane TaskRecord, the live generation and the retained Lane are unchanged. No test counts that the stop gate opens once on Claude Code or Pi. The stop semantics rest on each Host's applied predicate: Claude treats any non-throwing result other than replan_selected as applied, and Pi requires state === 'applied'. If a Host returns a cancelled result by value on Claude, stopSingleTaskSupervisor would terminate the generation although the user cancelled, and no test would catch it.",
        "caller_chain": [
          "tests/single-task-lane-decision.test.ts",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/unattended/lane_decision.ts#relayLaneDecision (stop branch)",
          "plugins/immune-brain/runtime/claude/kernel_ports.ts#ClaudeRuntime.authorize",
          "plugins/immune-brain/.pi-extension/imm-canary-work.ts#relayPiLaneDecision"
        ],
        "violated": {
          "kind": "acceptance",
          "ref": "DAL-S5-A2"
        }
      },
      "counterevidence": null
    },
